Both functions throw from deep inside, and the stacks are printed in a `.catch`. Why does the first stack show `c`, `async b` and `async a`, while the second shows only an anonymous frame?

```js
async function c() { await null; throw new Error('boom'); }
async function b() { await c(); }
async function a() { await b(); }

function c2() { return Promise.resolve().then(() => { throw new Error('boom2'); }); }
function b2() { return c2().then((x) => x); }
```

What does this print?

```js
